{
  "reasoning": "I treated the opening and recap as part of the first content sub-goal and kept the non-hand input material together because the later mention of 'category 4' and the final list of non-hand input methods depend on that context. I cut at explicit bridges where a finished topic is summarized and a new component is announced: input to processing at 37, processing to output at 66, visual displays to audio at 128, audio to haptics at 134, haptics to motion platforms/treadmills at 158, and main content to closing at 171. The output-device overview was merged with visual displays rather than made a standalone lecture-outline segment, and the closing summary/preview is its own final segment.",
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 1,
      "subgoal": "Explain the non-hand input methods in VR, with emphasis on full-body tracking and sound-based tracking, and summarize the four non-hand input categories."
    },
    {
      "start": 37,
      "subgoal": "Describe the processing/computer component of a VR system, including selection factors and the roles of GPU, CPU, and RAM."
    },
    {
      "start": 66,
      "subgoal": "Describe the main categories of VR output devices and explain the three types of visual displays (HMDs, world-fixed, and regular displays)."
    },
    {
      "start": 128,
      "subgoal": "Explain how audio output devices support spatial and immersive sound in VR."
    },
    {
      "start": 134,
      "subgoal": "Describe the main distinctions among haptic output devices, such as passive/active, tactile/proprioceptive, and self-grounded/world-grounded."
    },
    {
      "start": 158,
      "subgoal": "Explain motion platforms and treadmills as VR output devices, including active and passive variants."
    },
    {
      "start": 171,
      "subgoal": "Summarize the main points of the lecture and preview the next lecture on AR hardware."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "reasoning": "Segment 4 (audio output) was too narrow as a standalone sub-goal, and segment 6 (motion platforms and treadmills) was also narrow. I merged both with the adjacent haptics segment into one segment covering the main non-visual VR output devices: audio, haptics, motion platforms, and treadmills. This creates a more meaningful learner step while still ending before the closing summary. I kept the other cuts at the bridges where one major VR hardware component is closed and the next is introduced: non-hand input to processing at 37, processing to output at 66, visual displays to non-visual output at 128, and main content to closing at 171.",
  "segments": [
